> i think your general point is sound here, but I'll nitpick the statement
> that
> "if the server recognises an identity but is unable to verify correspondi=
ng
> binder".
>=20
> 1. The server only picks one identity so you if you send A, B, and C and =
you
> get an abort, you don't know if it recognized one or all.
> 2. The server can *recognize* the identity but ignore it (say it's a tick=
et
> that's
> too old)
>=20
> With that said, I think it would probably be safe to say you must ignore =
an
> identity
> where the binder doesn't validate, but I'd like to hear from cryptographe=
rs
> on this
> one.

Proposed https://github.com/tlswg/tls13-spec/pull/1167 so that we don't for=
get=20
about it.
=20
